 "final_text": "Submitted. Here's the tie-out for Sam:\n\n| | Amount |\n|---|---|\n| **We say CES Direct owes us** (parent AR, ERP acct IC-001) | **$76,500** |\n| **CES Direct says they owe us** (their Feb intercompany schedule) | **$54,000** |\n| **Difference** | **$22,500** |\n\n**Cause:** Three intercompany invoices make up the parent's $76,500 \u2014 ICINV-01 ($30,000, shared services Q4), ICINV-02 ($24,000, January inventory transfer), and ICINV-03 ($22,500, February management fee, dated 2026-02-27). CES Direct's schedule only shows the first two as booked ($54,000 total). Per an email from Dana Kim (CES contact), ICINV-03 didn't arrive at CES until 2026-03-01 \u2014 after their Feb close \u2014 so it's sitting in transit and will post to their books in March.\n\nBottom line: not a dispute, just a timing cutoff difference. The $22,500 gap is exactly ICINV-03; everything else ties out dollar-for-dollar.",
